<section class="content">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="content-text">
<p>This is the book of the chronicles of man, pure utterances, which we have heard from the mouth of our holy teacher, the hidden and concealed light, Rebbe Nachman, of blessed memory (zts"l). His awe-inspiring teachings were already published in the book Likutay Moharan, which has been printed previously.</p>

<p>These are his later words, which he added, innovated, and revealed after the completion of the aforementioned book. All that we heard from his holy mouth from that day forward until his passing is recorded in this book.</p>

<p>Know this: All the words of this book, as well as all the words of the first book already printed, are lofty matters, deep and vast beyond the sea. The seeker will weary himself to grasp their essence. Even on their simple level, it is exceedingly difficult to understand these words in writing, for they are profoundly deep matters.</p>

<p>However, it must be declared to all our brethren who tremble at the words of our Rebbe, of blessed memory—those who eagerly await and yearn to hear his words—that the primary intent of the teachings of our Rebbe, the hidden light, of blessed memory, which issued in holiness and purity from his sacred mouth, is not the exposition but the practice.</p>

<p>All his holy words are wondrous guidance, awe-inspiring counsel, and a great awakening to the service of Hashem, blessed be He. His words are like burning coals, blazing torches, kindling the heart with great fervor and intense yearning for Him, blessed be He.</p>

<p>The main intent of all his holy words is to draw a person closer to the service of Hashem, to reveal the path of truth, and to guide each soul according to its unique nature and level.</p>

<p>May we merit to fulfill all his words, which he spoke to us extensively in many ways—whether through public teachings, conversations with the masses, or numerous private conversations with each individual.</p>

<p>Amen, may it be His will.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
